# Long-term caching for the build output (docs/architecture/BUNDLE_BOUNDARIES.md).
#
# Every file Vite writes here carries a content hash in its name
# (index-ARoA8p5K.js): a new build produces NEW names, so a browser may keep
# these forever without ever serving stale code. Without this rule the server
# answered « no-store » and every visit re-downloaded the whole application.
#
# It lives in assets/ on purpose: a rule in the web root's .htaccess would be
# inherited by api/, whose responses must never be cached this way.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
</IfModule>
